   "html": "<div class=\"r \" style=\"--i:0\"><span class=\"chip\">Healthcare Innovation</span></div><div class=\"r \" style=\"--i:1\"><h1 class=\"title-long\"><span class=\"w\"><span style=\"--k:0\">An</span></span> <span class=\"w\"><span style=\"--k:1\">exploratory</span></span> <span class=\"w\"><span style=\"--k:2\">multi-scale</span></span> <span class=\"w\"><span style=\"--k:3\">analysis</span></span> <span class=\"w\"><span style=\"--k:4\">linking</span></span> <span class=\"w\"><span style=\"--k:5\">MRI</span></span> <span class=\"w\"><span style=\"--k:6\">radiomics</span></span> <span class=\"w\"><span style=\"--k:7\">with</span></span> <mark class=\"wipe-hl\"><span class=\"w\"><span style=\"--k:8\">KDR/VEGFR-2</span></span></mark> <span class=\"w\"><span style=\"--k:9\">expression</span></span> <span class=\"w\"><span style=\"--k:10\">and</span></span> <span class=\"w\"><span style=\"--k:11\">kinase-domain</span></span> <span class=\"w\"><span style=\"--k:12\">structure</span></span> <span class=\"w\"><span style=\"--k:13\">in</span></span> <span class=\"w\"><span style=\"--k:14\">glioblastoma</span></span></h1></div><div class=\"r \" style=\"--i:2\"><p class=\"byline\"><strong>Muhammad Dandy Nugraha · Wisnu Ananta Kusuma</strong><br><span>Department of Bioinformatics, IPB University</span></p></div><div class=\"r \" style=\"--i:3\"><div class=\"stat card\"><span class=\"num\">15 months</span><span class=\"lbl\">median survival, glioblastoma</span></div></div><div class=\"r foot\" style=\"--i:4\"><p class=\"credit\">Background: illustrative animation, not data.</p></div>",
   "notes": "Good morning everyone, and thank you to Chiang Mai University for having us. My name is Dandy, from IPB University in Indonesia, and this is work with my supervisor, Professor Wisnu Ananta Kusuma. The full title is on the screen. Fifteen months.   [jeda] That is how long most people live after they are told they have this brain cancer. It is called glioblastoma, and it is the most dangerous one we know. There is one drug that helps some of these patients. For the rest, it does nothing. And today, the only way to find out which group a patient is in is surgery. Someone has to open the skull, take a piece of the tumour, and send it to a lab.   [jeda] But every one of these patients has already had an MRI scan. So the question my supervisor and I asked was simple. Is the answer already inside that picture?",
   "notes_id": "Selamat pagi semuanya, dan terima kasih kepada Chiang Mai University yang sudah menjadi tuan rumah. Nama saya Dandy, dari IPB University, Indonesia, dan ini pekerjaan bersama pembimbing saya, Prof. Wisnu Ananta Kusuma. Judul lengkapnya ada di layar. Lima belas bulan.   [jeda] Itu lama hidup kebanyakan orang setelah diberi tahu bahwa mereka mengidap kanker otak ini. Namanya glioblastoma, dan itu yang paling berbahaya yang kita kenal. Ada satu obat yang membantu sebagian pasien. Untuk sisanya, obat itu tidak berpengaruh sama sekali. Dan hari ini, satu-satunya cara mengetahui seorang pasien masuk kelompok yang mana adalah operasi. Harus ada yang membuka tengkoraknya, mengambil potongan tumornya, lalu mengirimnya ke laboratorium.   [jeda] Padahal setiap pasien itu sudah pernah menjalani MRI. Jadi pertanyaan yang saya dan pembimbing saya ajukan sederhana. Apakah jawabannya sudah ada di dalam gambar itu?",
