   "title": "Measure KDR from an MRI, not from tissue.",
   "label": "The question",
   "html": "<div class=\"r \" style=\"--i:0\"><span class=\"chip\">The question</span></div><div class=\"r \" style=\"--i:1\"><h1 class=\"h1\">Measure KDR from an MRI, <mark class=\"wipe-hl\">not from tissue.</mark></h1></div><div class=\"r \" style=\"--i:2\"><div class=\"row2\"><div class=\"card \"><h3>Bevacizumab</h3><p>Blocks the signal that grows new blood vessels into the tumour.</p></div><div class=\"card \"><h3>VEGFR-2 · KDR</h3><p>The receiver, and the gene that builds it.</p></div></div></div><div class=\"r \" style=\"--i:3\"><div class=\"big-n\"><span class=\"num\" data-count=\"91\">91</span><span class=\"lbl\">patients · all public data</span></div></div>",
   "notes": "The drug is called bevacizumab. It works by blocking the signal that tells the body to grow new blood vessels into the tumour. It can only help patients whose tumour has many receivers for that signal. That receiver is called VEGFR-2. The gene that builds it is called KDR. So our goal was simple. Measure KDR from an MRI, not from tissue. Ninety one patients. All public data. No new scans, no new procedures, nothing a hospital does not already have.",
   "notes_id": "Obatnya bernama bevacizumab. Cara kerjanya memblokir sinyal yang menyuruh tubuh menumbuhkan pembuluh darah baru ke dalam tumor. Obat ini hanya bisa membantu pasien yang tumornya punya banyak penerima sinyal itu. Penerima itu namanya VEGFR-2. Gen yang membangunnya bernama KDR. Jadi tujuan kami sederhana. Mengukur KDR dari MRI, bukan dari jaringan. Sembilan puluh satu pasien. Semuanya data publik. Tidak ada pemindaian baru, tidak ada prosedur baru, tidak ada yang belum dimiliki rumah sakit.",
   "bridge": "But before the method, you need to know why we chose the receiver.",
   "direction": "Tempo naik sedikit. Ini bagian teknis pertama, sebut namanya dengan jelas dan jangan buru-buru.",
