   "label": "Methods",
   "html": "<div class=\"r \" style=\"--i:0\"><span class=\"chip\">Methods</span></div><div class=\"r \" style=\"--i:1\"><h1 class=\"h1\">Image, gene, structure.</h1></div><div class=\"stack\"><div class=\"r card line\" style=\"--i:2\"><span class=\"idx\">01</span><div><h3>Image</h3><p>PyRadiomics turns each MRI into measurements we can name.</p></div></div><div class=\"r card line\" style=\"--i:3\"><span class=\"idx\">02</span><div><h3>Gene</h3><p>Does it rise and fall together with KDR in the same patient?</p></div></div><div class=\"r card line\" style=\"--i:4\"><span class=\"idx\">03</span><div><h3>Structure</h3><p>A pocket where a drug can attach. VEGFR-2 kinase domain, PDB 2OH4.</p></div></div></div><div class=\"r \" style=\"--i:5\"><p class=\"aside\">Why not deep learning? Ninety one patients is far too few.</p></div>",
   "notes": "An MRI is already made of numbers. It is a grid of brightness values. Radiomics is software that reads that grid and gives back measurements we can name. How rough the edge of the tumour is. How round the shape is. Whether the brightness is even or uneven. One scan gives us about a thousand of these. Then for each one we ask a single question. Does it rise and fall together with KDR in the same patient? And if one does, we look at the protein, to check there is a pocket where a drug can attach. Image, gene, structure. That is the pipeline. People ask why we did not use deep learning. Ninety one patients is far too few. And a deep learning model cannot tell a doctor which part of the image it used.",
   "notes_id": "MRI itu sebenarnya sudah terbuat dari angka. Dia kisi-kisi nilai kecerahan. Radiomics adalah perangkat lunak yang membaca kisi itu lalu mengembalikan ukuran yang bisa kita beri nama. Seberapa kasar tepi tumornya. Seberapa bulat bentuknya. Kecerahannya merata atau tidak. Satu pemindaian memberi kita sekitar seribu ukuran. Lalu untuk tiap ukuran kami tanyakan satu hal. Apakah dia naik turun bersama KDR pada pasien yang sama? Dan kalau ada yang begitu, kami lihat proteinnya, untuk memastikan ada kantong tempat obat bisa menempel. Citra, gen, struktur. Itu alurnya. Orang bertanya kenapa kami tidak pakai deep learning. Sembilan puluh satu pasien jauh terlalu sedikit. Dan model deep learning tidak bisa memberi tahu dokter bagian mana dari gambar yang dia pakai.",
   "bridge": "So far the method looks clean. And this is where I almost got it wrong.",
   "direction": "Ini jawaban untuk pertanyaan soal PyRadiomics. Tiga langkah, hitung pakai jari kalau perlu.",
